2.5 LOGISTIC-NORMAL ACTOR-CRITIC
--------------------------------
Cheridito & Weiss (2025):
- Novel RL framework for LOB execution
- Dynamic allocation: optimal placement of MARKET and LIMIT orders
- Multivariate logistic-normal distributions
- Efficient training of RL algorithm
- Outperforms traditional benchmark strategies

Mathematical Framework:
    Policy parameterization on (K+1)-simplex:
        h(x)_k = exp(x_k) / (1 + Σⱼ exp(xⱼ)), for k = 0,...,K-1
        h(x)_k = 1 / (1 + Σⱼ exp(xⱼ)), for k = K

Reward Structure:
    r = r̄ - γₙ × p_b(0) / M₀
    where: r̄ = cash flow from executed trades
           γₙ = lots sold in step n
           p_b(0) = initial best bid price
           M₀ = initial inventory

REF: Cheridito & Weiss (2025) "Reinforcement Learning for Trade Execution"
