6. MARKET IMPACT MODELING
==========================

6.1 IMPACT COMPONENTS
---------------------
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Impact Type           │ Description                                    │
├───────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Permanent Impact      │ Price change that persists after execution    │
│ Temporary Impact      │ Price change that decays over time            │
│ Transient Impact      │ Impact with resilience (LOB recovery)         │
│ Endogenous Impact     │ Impact that depends on agent's own actions    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

REF: Almgren & Chriss (2001)
     Gatheral & Schied (2011)
     RL-Exec (Duflot & Robineau, 2025)

6.2 IMPACT MODEL PARAMETERS
---------------------------
Almgren-Chriss Model:
    Permanent Impact: γ × x_t
    Temporary Impact: η × (x_t / V_t)
    where: x_t = trade size at time t
           V_t = volume at time t
           γ = permanent impact coefficient
           η = temporary impact coefficient

RL-Exec Impact Model:
    - Endogenous transient impact with resilience
    - Parametric impact process calibrated to historical data
    - Partial fill modeling

REF: Almgren & Chriss (2001)
     RL-Exec (Duflot & Robineau, 2025)

